That's a reference to a common format for a Javadoc comment in Java programming language. It's used to document classes, methods or variables with a description of their purpose or usage.

For example:

```java
/**
 * <<title>>
 * This is a class that handles user authentication.
 */
public class Authenticator {
    //...
}
```

In this case, the title is usually a short description of the purpose of the class or method.

Another example:

```java
/**
 * <<title>>
 * This method handles the deletion of a user account.
 */
public void deleteUser() {
    //...
}
```

In this case, the title is a short description of what the method does.

This format is often used in conjunction with tools like Javadoc that can extract the title and display it as a tooltip or help text when you hover over the method or variable name in an IDE.

